    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1587">

                <pb facs="1006" n="890" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg890"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/75.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Bevan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-18T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>German Embassy transmits report that Constitutionalists have confiscated
                    warehouse and goods of German firm Eversbusch at Tampico.</p>
                <p>Investigate and if report correct, use good offices to secure release of
                    property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
